If the formatter for your filetype isn\[cq]t installed, \f[CR]:fmt\f[R]
reports a status\-line error and leaves the buffer alone.
.SH Usage
.IP
.EX
:fmt              # format current buffer
.EE
.PP
A typical workflow: bind it to a key and call before saving.
With the default leader cluster, \f[CR]<space>cf\f[R] is wired to
\f[CR]:fmt\f[R].
.SH Notes
\f[CR]fmt\f[R] writes the buffer to disk first (if dirty), then runs the
formatter on the on\-disk file, then reloads.
If the formatter doesn\[cq]t support \f[CR]\-\-write\f[R]\-style
in\-place editing, this plugin won\[cq]t work for it as\-is \[em] patch
the formatter table in \f[CR]plugins/fmt/fmt.c\f[R] if you need a
different invocation pattern.
.PP
The formatter table is hardcoded (see the project roadmap \[em] making
it user\-configurable is on the list).
To add a filetype, edit the table and rebuild.
